      "content": "Signalized intersections use traffic lights to regulate vehicle and pedestrian movements, which can lead to delays during peak hours if not optimally timed. Roundabouts, on the other hand, can improve traffic flow by allowing continuous movement around a central island, usually resulting in smoother traffic throughput and less stop-and-go situations during high traffic volumes. During peak hours, roundabouts tend to better handle large volumes of traffic with reduced delay times compared to signalized intersections.",
